var A=[{"s": "sop", "c": "Applications", "d": "Sep 22, 2026", "r": "5 min", "t": "How to write a statement of purpose that gets read", "x": "Admissions teams read hundreds. Here is a simple structure that keeps yours clear and personal.", "b": ["Start with one specific moment that pushed you toward your subject. A project, a job, a problem you could not stop thinking about. Avoid opening with a general line about education changing the world.", "Then connect your past to the course. Name two or three modules or research areas at that university and say why they fit your plan. This shows you chose the course, not just the country.", "Close with what you will do after graduating. Keep it to one page and one voice, and have a counsellor or teacher read it before you submit."]}, {"s": "ielts-pte", "c": "Tests", "d": "Sep 15, 2026", "r": "4 min", "t": "IELTS or PTE: how to choose", "x": "Both are widely accepted. The better test is the one that suits how you perform.", "b": ["IELTS has a face-to-face speaking test and paper or computer options. PTE is fully computer based and scored by software, which many students find more predictable.", "Check the exact test and score your university and visa route accept before booking. Some courses ask for higher scores in writing or speaking.", "Take one practice test of each. Pick the format where you feel calmer and score higher, then plan four to eight weeks of focused preparation."]}, {"s": "visa-mistakes", "c": "Visas", "d": "Sep 8, 2026", "r": "4 min", "t": "Five document mistakes that delay student visas", "x": "Most delays come from small, avoidable errors in the file, not from weak profiles.", "b": ["Names that differ between passport, transcripts and bank papers cause questions. Make them match, or bring a supporting document that explains the difference.", "Funds shown without a clear history, or in an account that is not accepted, are another common problem. Read the funds rules for your country closely.", "Expired or missing tests, unsigned forms and low-quality scans complete the list. Build a checklist and let someone review it before you submit."]}, {"s": "scholarships", "c": "Funding", "d": "Aug 30, 2026", "r": "6 min", "t": "A simple plan to find scholarships for your master’s", "x": "Funding is easier to win when you start early and apply to several sources.", "b": ["Begin with government schemes, then look at university awards and country-specific programmes. Write down each deadline and required document in one sheet.", "Reuse your core story, but tailor every essay to the scholarship’s goals. Reviewers can tell when an essay is generic.", "Ask referees early and give them your CV and a short brief. Strong references often decide close cases."]}, {"s": "first-month", "c": "Life abroad", "d": "Aug 21, 2026", "r": "5 min", "t": "Your first month abroad: a practical checklist", "x": "The first weeks set the tone. Sort these basics early and the rest gets easier.", "b": ["Before you fly, save digital copies of all documents, confirm airport pickup or directions, and carry enough cash and a working card for the first few days.", "In week one, collect your student card, open a bank account, set up a local SIM and register with your university and a doctor.", "Join a society or community group early. Friends and local tips do more for settling in than any guide."]}]
